    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42188" root="وفض" body-key="w">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفْضٌ</span></b>  (S, M, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفَضٌ</span></b>  (M, K) <i>Haste:</i>
(S, M, K:) [like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفْزٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفَزٌ</span>:] pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْفَاضٌ</span>. (K.)
You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَآءَ عَلَى وَفْضٍ</span>, and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَفَضٍ</span></b> , and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْفَاضٍ</span>,
<i>He came in haste.</i> (M.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِيتُهُ عَلَى أَوْفَاضٍ</span>
<i>I found him in a state of haste:</i> (S, K:) like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْفَازٍ</span>. (S.)

